    "created_at": "2026-01-19T18:40:23Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-19T18:40:23Z",
    "body": "I think that's fair; the bytemask algorithm is very heavy-handed.\n\nIt should be noted, however, that the spec explicitly scopes this pattern to situations when sniffing for fonts explicitly. The \"font type pattern matching algorithm\" is only ever used by \"rules for sniffing fonts specifically\", which is an algorithm hook that was designed by things like CSS's `@font-face` but is not to my knowledge used by any standard.\n\nIt looks like Go is including the font patterns when sniffing in a browsing context, which is in contradiction to the spec:\nhttps://github.com/golang/go/blob/7251c9e0f00a6d7d37bb441f3e823c160131e9b5/src/net/http/sniff.go#L66-L195",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
